- All dialogs, modals, and popups in the application must follow the enterprise/professional UI design standards.
- When creating or updating any dialog, automatically apply the following structure:

## Standard Dialog Structure

### 1. Dialog Container

```tsx
<Dialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={setIsOpen}>
  <DialogContent className="max-w-[600px] p-0 max-h-[90vh] flex flex-col overflow-hidden border border-slate-200 shadow-xl">
    {/* Professional Cap */}
    <div className="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 bg-[#d6d7d8] opacity-70 rounded-t-md" />

    {/* Header with gradient background */}
    <div className="sticky top-0 z-10 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 py-4 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div className="flex items-center gap-3 px-6">
        {/* Icon with circular background */}
        <div className="w-8 h-8 bg-blue-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
          <IconComponent className="w-5 h-5 text-blue-600" />
        </div>

        {/* Title */}
        <div>
          <DialogTitle className="text-xl font-semibold sidebar-gradient-text">
            Dialog Title
          </DialogTitle>
          <p className="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
            Optional subtitle or description
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Scrollable Content */}
    <div className="flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-6 bg-white">
      {/* Main content here */}
    </div>

    {/* Professional Footer */}
    <div className="px-6 py-4 bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200 flex items-center justify-between">
      <div className="text-xs text-slate-500">Optional footer text</div>
      <div className="flex items-center gap-3">
        <Button variant="outline" className="primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4">
          Cancel
        </Button>
        <Button className="primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4">Action</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## Required Design Elements

### Professional Cap

- Always include a thin horizontal bar at the top: `<div className="absolute top-0 left-0 right-0 h-4 bg-[#d6d7d8] opacity-70 rounded-t-md" />`
- This creates visual consistency and indicates an enterprise application

### Header Section

- Use gradient background: `bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50`
- Include a prominent icon in a circular colored background
- Title uses `sidebar-gradient-text` for brand consistency
- Subtitle uses `text-sm text-slate-600` for hierarchy

### Content Section

- Scrollable area with `flex-1 overflow-y-auto p-6 bg-white`
- Use adequate padding (p-6 or p-4) for breathing room
- Group related content in cards with `bg-slate-50 rounded-lg p-4 border border-slate-200`

### Footer Section

- Background: `bg-slate-50 border-t border-slate-200`
- Include helpful text and action buttons
- Use consistent button styling: `primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4`

## Interactive Elements

### Hoverable Cards/Items

- Use subtle hover effects: `hover:bg-blue-50 hover:border-blue-300 transition-all duration-200`
- Add shadow on hover for depth: `shadow-sm hover:shadow-md`
- Use `group` class for coordinated hover states on parent and children

### Icons

- Use consistent icon sizing: `h-4 w-4` or `h-5 w-5` for most icons
- Colored icons: `text-blue-600`, `text-green`, `text-slate-600` etc.
- Circular icon backgrounds: `w-8 h-8 bg-blue-100 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center`

### Buttons

- Primary action buttons: `className="primary-btn px-3 sm:px-4"`
- Include icons in buttons when appropriate
- Use consistent spacing: `gap-3` between buttons

## Color Palette

- Primary: Blue gradient (from-blue-50 to-indigo-50)
- Background: White (bg-white) with slate-50 for sections
- Borders: slate-200
- Text:
  - Primary: slate-900
  - Secondary: slate-600
  - Muted: slate-500
  - Headers: sidebar-gradient-text (brand colors)
- Accents: blue-600, green, purple-600

## List/Event Items in Dialogs

When displaying lists or events in dialogs:

- Use cards with border-2 for emphasis
- Include gradient icon backgrounds
- Show metadata with icons (Clock, Users, etc.)
- Add chevron indicators for clickable items
- Use badges/tags for categories or status

Example structure:

```tsx
<button className="w-full text-left p-4 rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-200 bg-white hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50 transition-all duration-200 group shadow-sm hover:shadow-md">
  <div className="flex items-start gap-4">
    {/* Icon */}
    <div className="w-10 h-10 bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-100 to-indigo-100 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 group-hover:from-blue-200 group-hover:to-indigo-200 transition-colors">
      <Icon className="h-5 w-5 text-blue-600" />
    </div>

    {/* Content */}
    <div className="flex-1 min-w-0">{/* Title and metadata */}</div>

    {/* Indicator */}
    <ChevronRight className="h-5 w-5 text-slate-400 group-hover:text-blue-600 transition-colors" />
  </div>
</button>
```

## Consistency Requirements

- NEVER use plain DialogContent without the professional structure
- NEVER skip the cap bar at the top
- NEVER use flat backgrounds in headers - always use the gradient
- NEVER forget to make content areas scrollable for overflow
- ALWAYS include footer sections with proper background and borders
- ALWAYS use consistent spacing and padding throughout
- ALWAYS apply transition effects for interactive elements

